  "description": "LUYCEO crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C86 H103 Ce3 N6 O23 S8,2.5(C3 H7 N1 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 4 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 5 O neighbors; Ce1A (Ce) has 4 O neighbors; Ce2A (Ce) has 5 O neighbors; Ce2E (Ce) has 5 O neighbors; Ce2D (Ce) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 0.682-4.876 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 16.08-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C86H103Ce3N6O23S8·2.5(dmf).",
